# ============================================================================
#  The kit (world expansion 1, K2): what a student can own and wear.
#  One wand, one robe and one trinket are worn; worn effects act in fights only, as flat numbers. Owning an item
#  adds options to cards where it fits (`> up[item:x]:`). Amounts in `price:` are what the pawnbroker pays.
#  Format: docs/grimoire-script.md (@item). Where each comes from: the plan's K2 table and the events that give them.
# ============================================================================

# ---------------- Wands ----------------

@item borrowed_wand
name: Borrowed Wand
slot: wand
art: wand
start: true
desc: The academy's loan to every first-year: scuffed beech, a chipped tip and somebody else's initials on the handle. It works. Mostly.

@item hazel_wand
name: Hazelwood Wand
slot: wand
art: wand
price: small
worn: mana +1
desc: Mir's work: light, springy hazel with a copper band. It warms up before you do.

@item ashwood_wand
name: Ashwood Duelling Wand
slot: wand
art: wand
price: medium
worn: on_defend strike 2
desc: A duellist's wand, dense and unforgiving. Anything that tries to block it gets a shock for its trouble.

@item heartwood_wand
name: Heartwood Wand
slot: wand
art: wand
price: medium
worn: mana +2
desc: Carved by Mir from a splinter the elder oak gave you. The grain moves when no one is looking.

@item edmunds_silver_wand
name: Edmund's Silver Wand
slot: wand
art: wand
legacy: flag(edmunds_wand)
worn: cost ward -2
desc: Slender silver, sixty years old, wrapped for decades in a faded scarf. Near the lake it hums one low note.

@item thorn_wand
name: Thorn Wand
slot: wand
art: wand
worn: on_cast forbidden spell 2
desc: Blackthorn, still bristling, still faintly green at the core. It wants to be used, and it does not much care for what.
tick:
  alignment -tiny
  say: {~The thorn wand pricks your palm when you pick it up, as if it were keeping count.|You dream of brambles growing over a door. The thorn wand is warm in the morning.}

# ---------------- Robes ----------------

@item school_robes
name: School Robes
slot: robe
art: mask
start: true
price: tiny
desc: Regulation black with the house trim, a size too big in the sleeves. Everyone has a pair.

@item duelling_coat
name: Quilted Duelling Coat
slot: robe
art: shield
price: small
worn: hp +3, cost brace -1
desc: Padded, stitched in diamonds, smelling faintly of the duelling hall. Bracing in it feels like leaning on a wall.

@item ward_cloak
name: Ward-Stitched Cloak
slot: robe
art: shield
price: medium
worn: hp +2, taken -2 from flame hoarfrost starlight
desc: Amaranth's ward thread runs through the hem in a pattern too fine to see. Fire and frost slide off it like rain.

@item midnight_robes
name: Midnight-Blue Robes
slot: robe
art: crown
price: small
worn: hp +2
desc: Deep blue wool with silver trim and a lining like the night sky. People stand up a little straighter when you walk in.

@item spinner_silk_robe
name: Spinner-Silk Robe
slot: robe
art: spider
price: large
worn: hp +6, cost shadowstep -1, cost haste -1
desc: Grey silk that drinks the light, sewn by the village tailor from what the Spinner left you. You move in it like a rumour.

# ---------------- Trinkets ----------------

@item ilse_frost_ward
name: Ilse's Frost-Ward
slot: trinket
art: snow
legacy: has(frost_ward)
worn: taken -2 from flame wildfire
desc: A sliver of Northern winter that Ilse sewed into your collar. Cold things think twice about you.
tick:
  arcana +1
  health +1

@item black_star_coin
name: Black-Star Coin
slot: trinket
art: coin
legacy: flag(star_coin)
bound: true
worn: cost umbral -1, cost forbidden -1
desc: Black, cold as ice and heavier than it should be, stamped with a hollow star. You keep meaning to throw it away.

@item lodestone_pendant
name: Lodestone Pendant
slot: trinket
art: compass
price: small
desc: A dark stone on a leather cord that turns, very slowly, to face north. In the Whisperwood it is never wrong.

@item stag_tine
name: Stag's Tine
slot: trinket
art: paw
price: small
worn: taken -2 from nonhuman
desc: A tine shed by the shadow stag, smooth as old ivory. Wild things look at it before they look at you.

@item owl_quill
name: Owl-Feather Quill
slot: trinket
art: feather
price: tiny
desc: A barn-owl feather cut to a nib. Notes taken with it are tidier than the hand that wrote them.

@item moonpetal_locket
name: Moonpetal Locket
slot: trinket
art: moon
price: medium
worn: mana +2
desc: A plain silver locket with one pressed moonpetal inside. It opens on its own at midnight.

@item pocket_almanac
name: Pocket Almanac
slot: trinket
art: book
price: tiny
desc: Tides, moons and weather for fifty years, in print you need a lens for. Grimsby's pencil notes run down every margin.

@item measuring_spoon
name: Pell's Measuring Spoon
slot: trinket
art: potion
desc: A brass spoon worn thin on one side by forty years of exact quarters. Pell's daughters say it is theirs.

@item honey_tin
name: Honey Tin
slot: trinket
art: flower
desc: A dented tin of Maud's silver-bee honey. Shared, it opens doors; the bees seem to know it is yours.

@item outcast_grimoire
name: The Outcast's Grimoire
slot: trinket
art: book
worn: cost forbidden -2, on_cast forbidden spell 2
desc: A black-bound book of forbidden practice in a cramped, elegant hand. Its pages are cold, and some of them are blank until midnight.

# ---------------- The capital (maps round 2, S1) ----------------
# Sold in the capital: the wandwright's in the Arcade of Services (the wands), the Grand Bazaar (the rest), its curio
# stall one piece per visit in turn. Each is worth its price for a worn effect nothing else gives, or for the options it
# opens on other cards (`up[item:…]`), listed in docs/maps-plan.md (S1).

@item glasscore_wand
name: Glasscore Wand
slot: wand
art: wand
price: medium
worn: on_cast any spell 1
desc: Pale birch around a thread of capital glass, from the wandwright in the Arcade of Services. Every spell you cast through it throws a spark of its own.

@item tidewood_wand
name: Tidewood Wand
slot: wand
art: wand
price: small
worn: cost ward -1, taken -1 from flame
desc: Driftwood from the Port Calder breakwater, salt-hardened and re-cored by the wandwright. Wards come off it smooth as a wave going out, and fire hisses out against it.

@item oilskin_coat
name: Courier's Oilskin
slot: robe
art: rain
price: small
worn: hp +2, cost tailwind -1
desc: A long waxed coat of the kind the capital's couriers wear, with a hood like a coal-scuttle. Rain gives up on it.

@item duellist_silk
name: Duellist's Silk
slot: robe
art: duel
price: medium
worn: hp +1, cost haste -1, on_defend strike 1
desc: Close-cut grey silk from the bazaar's fencing-master's stall, made for the capital's dawn duels. It moves before you do, and stings whatever blocks you.

@item lockpick_roll
name: Lockpick Roll
slot: trinket
art: key
price: small
desc: A roll of soft leather with eleven picks and a tension wrench, sold at the bazaar "for locksmiths". The seller didn't ask whether you were one.

@item pocket_orrery
name: Pocket Orrery
slot: trinket
art: planet
price: medium
worn: cost starlight -1, cost lodestar -1
desc: A brass orrery the size of a walnut, wound with a key. Its planets keep the true sky's time, clouds or no clouds.

@item storm_glass
name: Storm-Glass
slot: trinket
art: rain
price: small
worn: taken -1 from forbidden
desc: A sealed glass tear of camphor and salts that clouds before weather turns. Forbidden things, the stall-keeper swore, cloud it too.

@item ivory_dice
name: Gambler's Ivory Dice
slot: trinket
art: cards
price: small
desc: A pair of old ivory dice from the bazaar's curio stall, yellow as teeth. They aren't loaded. They're only lucky, which the curio-seller says is worse.

@item clockwork_songbird
name: Clockwork Songbird
slot: trinket
art: feather
price: small
worn: mana +1
desc: A brass linnet from the curio stall, with a key in its back and twelve songs in its chest. It sings the thirteenth when it thinks it's alone.

@item sea_glass_charm
name: Sea-Glass Charm
slot: trinket
art: snow
price: medium
worn: hp +2, taken -1 from hoarfrost rime
desc: A green knot of sea-glass on a sailor's cord, from the curio stall. It is always cold, and colder things leave it alone.

# ---------------- The countryside (maps round 2, K5) ----------------
# Sold at the country market in the market village.

@item waxed_cloak
name: Waxed Cloak
slot: robe
art: rain
price: small
worn: hp +3, taken -1 from creature
desc: Heavy waxed wool from the market village, smelling of sheep and rain. The wind off the moor gives up on it.

@item shepherds_crook
name: Shepherd's Crook
slot: trinket
art: paw
price: tiny
desc: Seasoned ash with a horn handle, cut an inch short for stooping. On the moor's bog roads it feels the soft ground before you do: one fall more you can survive.
